%erg 0.1
Title: erg migrate: prune orphan ticket-* skills and stale prose from old host installs
Created: 2026-06-11
Author: Claude

--- log ---
2026-06-11T08:30Z Claude created
2026-06-11T08:30Z Claude note transcribed from AEDIST tickets/0355 (filed 2026-05-27 when that agent had no git-erg access)
2026-06-11T09:00Z Claude note retargeted from erg update to erg migrate: update's contract is binary-only (never writes store files), while migrateLayout is already the home for one-time legacy-install cleanup (removes tickets/tools/, content-rewrites pre-commit hooks, refreshes AGENTS.md, never commits). Added .claude/settings.json hook-command rewrite to scope (AEDIST tickets/0526 evidence was already cited but unactioned).

--- body ---
## Context

Early `erg init` bundles (pre spec 0.1; e.g. AEDIST PR #570, 2026-05-25)
vendored five `.claude/skills/ticket-{new,claim,close,ready,release}/`
skills into host repos, plus a managed CLAUDE.md block claiming "no CLI
needed" and pointing the validator at `tickets/tools/go/`. Those skills
duplicated `erg <verb>` in prose and drifted: they described `%erg v1`
with a `Status:` header, which the 0.1 validator rejects.

The current source no longer ships any of this. But existing host
installs keep the orphans until someone hand-deletes them (AEDIST had
to: commit bbd2670d), and stale hook commands like
`tickets/tools/go/erg validate tickets/` linger in host
`.claude/settings.json` (AEDIST tickets/0526).

## Actions

All in `erg migrate` (the layout step, which already runs only when DIR is
the canonical `tickets/` and already removes tickets/tools/, content-rewrites
the pre-commit hook, and refreshes AGENTS.md — same vintage of cleanup):

1. Detect and remove previously-vendored `.claude/skills/ticket-*` dirs.
   Those bundles predate provenance markers, so match the known vendored
   content — tell-tale legacy substrings (`%erg v1`, `Status:` header
   prose) rather than exact hashes, since hosts may carry minor local
   edits. Only delete when the tell-tale content is present.
2. Rewrite/refresh the managed `# --- git-erg ---` CLAUDE.md block if
   present, dropping "no CLI needed" / `tickets/tools/go/` / `%erg v1`
   claims.
3. Rewrite stale hook commands in host `.claude/settings.json` (and any
   other hook-definition files we vendor into): `tickets/tools/go/erg`
   -> `tickets/erg`, `validate tickets/` -> `check tickets/` — the same
   content-based, idempotent rewrite migrateHook applies to
   .git/hooks/pre-commit (AEDIST tickets/0526).
4. Emit a one-line notice for each artifact pruned or rewritten.
5. Optionally, `erg update` may *detect* the orphans post-swap and print
   "run erg migrate" guidance (parallel to its Status:-header hint), but
   it never mutates them itself.

## Test

First (red) test: install the old bundle (skills present, stale
CLAUDE.md block, .claude/settings.json hooks referencing
tickets/tools/go/erg) into a scratch repo, run `erg migrate tickets`,
assert the `.claude/skills/ticket-*` directories are gone, the managed
block no longer mentions skills or `%erg v1`, and settings.json hooks
reference `tickets/erg ... check tickets/`.

## Invariants

- `erg migrate` never touches skills, CLAUDE.md, or settings.json
  content outside the git-erg managed blocks / known vendored content
  (skill dirs without the tell-tale legacy content are left alone).
- Re-running `erg migrate` is idempotent.
- `erg update` keeps its binary-only contract: it may hint, never prune.
- Like the rest of migrate: never commits; user reviews the diff.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `erg migrate` removes previously-installed `ticket-*` skills from a
      host repo (verified on a scratch install of the old bundle).
- [ ] The managed CLAUDE.md block, when refreshed, references
      `erg <verb>` and `%erg 0.1`, with no "no CLI needed" /
      `tickets/tools/go/` claims.
- [ ] Stale `tickets/tools/go/erg` / `validate tickets/` hook commands in
      `.claude/settings.json` are rewritten to `tickets/erg` /
      `check tickets/`.
- [ ] Scratch-repo migrate test passes and is idempotent.
